hadiths[250]{hadithnumber,text}:
"250","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: Do not be among those who are hasty, those who spread indecent talk, or those who disclose secrets. Very severe calamities that will distort faces are coming after you, and very long and extensive tribulations will arise which will be very burdensome."
"251","It is narrated from Abu Jubairah bin Dihhak, he said: These verses were revealed about us, the Banu Salamah: «ولا تنابزوا بالألقاب» [الحجرات: ۱۱] ""And do not call each other by offensive nicknames."" He said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) came to us, there was not a single person among us who did not have two names (one real and one distorted). So the Prophet (peace be upon him) began to say: ""O so-and-so!"" Then the people would say: O Messenger of Allah! He gets upset by that. (Because that is his distorted name, and that is the name you know him by.)"
"252","Ikrimah says: I do not know whether it was Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) or his cousin, which of the two prepared food for his companion? The situation was that a slave girl was working in front of them, when one of them said to the slave girl: ""O wicked one!"" The other said: ""Stop! If this slave girl cannot enforce the punishment on you in this world, she will enforce it in the Hereafter."" The other said: ""Please tell me, if this is really the case."" He said: ""Allah does not love those who speak foolishly or those who speak affectedly."" It was Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) who said this sentence: «إن الله لا يحب الفاحش المتفحش» ."
"253","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that a person was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so a man praised him well. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Alas, you have cut your companion's neck."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept repeating this. ""If any of you must praise someone, he should say: 'I think so-and-so is such and such,' if he thinks him to be so, and his reckoning is with Allah, and do not present anyone's purity before Allah."""
"254","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man praising another man and exaggerating in his praise, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You have destroyed him,"" or he said: ""You have broken your brother's back."" (That is, by praising, a person becomes lazy in action and corruption arises.)"
"255","Ibrahim Taimi narrates from his father, who said: We were sitting with Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) when a person praised another person in his presence. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: You have killed this man, may Allah kill you."
"256","Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Praising (someone) is (like) slaughtering him. Muhammad says: That is, when he accepts it."
"257","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Abu Bakr is a very good man, Umar is very good, Abu Ubaidah is a very good man, Usayd bin Hudayr is very good, likewise Thabit bin Qais bin Shammas is a very good man, Mu'adh bin Amr bin Jamuh is a very good man, Mu'adh bin Jabal is a very good man."" He said: ""And such-and-such a man is bad, and such-and-such a man is bad,"" until he counted seven men."
"258","It is narrated from Abu Muammar, he said: A man stood up and began to praise one of the rulers among the rulers, so Sayyiduna Miqdad (may Allah be pleased with him) started throwing dust on his face and said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to throw dust on the faces of those who praise others."
"259","Ata bin Abi Rabah narrates that a man was praising another person in the presence of Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them). So Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) took some soil and began to throw it towards his (the praiser’s) mouth and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “When you see those who praise others, throw dust in their faces.”"
"260","Muhjan al-Aslami said that Raja narrated: One day I was coming with Muhjan until we stopped at the mosque of the people of Basra, and Buraydah al-Aslami was sitting at one of the doors of the mosque. He says: And there was a man in the mosque whose name was Sakbah, and he used to pray for a very long time. When we reached the door of the mosque, Buraydah was wrapped in a cloak and he was a man who liked to joke and laugh. He said: O Muhjan! Do you pray like Sakbah prays? Muhjan did not answer him and turned back. Muhjan says: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) took my hand and we started walking until we climbed Mount Uhud, and he (peace and blessings be upon him) looked towards Madinah and said: ""Woe to this village, its inhabitants will abandon it when it is very populated. The Dajjal will come to it and he will find an angel at each of its gates, so he will not be able to enter it."" Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) descended. When we reached the mosque, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saw a man praying, bowing and prostrating repeatedly, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) asked me: ""Who is this?"" I began to praise him excessively. I said: O Messenger of Allah! He is so-and-so and so-and-so. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Stop, do not let him hear, otherwise you will destroy him."" It is narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) walked until he reached his apartments, but when he got there, he (peace and blessings be upon him) dusted off his hands and then said: ""The best of your religion is that which is easiest, the best of your religion is that which is easiest."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said this three times."
"261","Muhammad (bin Sirin) said that people used to say: Do not honor your friend so much that it becomes burdensome for him."
"262","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""When a person visits his brother who is ill or meets him, Allah Almighty says to him: You are blessed and your walking is blessed, and you have made a place for yourself in Paradise."""
"263","It is narrated from Sayyida Umm Darda’ (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: Salman al-Farisi came to meet us, traveling from Mada’in to Sham, in such a state that he was wearing a shirt and « انْدَرْوَرْدُ » (i.e., such trousers that were above the shins). Ibn Shawdhab said: Salman was seen wearing a shirt that had no collar and it was very long and loose. So it was said to him, “You have made yourself look unattractive.” He replied: “Indeed, the true goodness is the goodness of the Hereafter.”"
"264","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, visited a household of the Ansar and ate food with them. When he was about to leave, he instructed regarding a place in the house, so a mat was spread there and water was sprinkled on that mat. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, performed voluntary prayer on it and supplicated for them."
"265","Abu Khulda narrates that Abdul Karim Abu Umayyah came to Abu Aliah. At that time, he was wearing woolen clothes, so Abu Aliah said: This clothing is for monks; indeed, when Muslims used to meet each other, they would adorn themselves."
"266","It is narrated from Abdullah, the freed slave of Sayyida Asma’ (may Allah be pleased with her): Sayyida Asma’ (may Allah be pleased with her) showed me a cloak which the elders used to wear. Its collar was made of thick silk and its sleeves were adorned with silk embroidery. Sayyida Asma’ (may Allah be pleased with her) said: This is the cloak of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), which he used to wear when delegations arrived and on Fridays."
"267","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that he stated: Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) received a cloak made of thick silk. He took it to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah! Buy this and wear it on Fridays and when distinguished people come to you as a delegation. Upon this, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Such clothes are worn by those who have no share in the Hereafter."" Then some cloaks were brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). He sent one cloak to Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), one cloak to Sayyiduna Usama (may Allah be pleased with him), and one cloak to Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him). Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah! You have sent this to me while I have heard your statement about it? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Sell it or fulfill any other need with it."""
"268","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""A man set out to visit a brother of his in another town, so Allah appointed an angel to wait for him on his way. The angel asked: 'Where are you going?' He replied: 'To visit a brother of mine who lives in this town.' The angel asked: 'Has he done you any favor which you are going to repay?' He replied: 'No, I only love him for the sake of Allah.' The angel said: 'I am a messenger to you from Allah (to inform you) that Allah loves you as you love him.'"""
"269","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) that once I said: O Messenger of Allah! A person loves some people but it is not within his ability (through his actions) to reach their level. Upon this, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Abu Dharr! You will be with those whom you love."" I said: I love Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: ""O Abu Dharr! You will be with those whom you love."""
"270","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: ""O Messenger of Allah! When will the Hour (Day of Judgment) come?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What have you prepared for it?"" He replied: ""I have not prepared much for it, but I love Allah and His Messenger."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A person will be with those whom he loves."" Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) states that after embracing Islam, I never saw the Muslims as happy about anything as they were on that day (because of this statement)."
"271","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""He who does not show mercy to our young ones and does not recognize the right of respect of our elders is not from among us."""
"272","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with him) that he reports this hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in a marfu’ form, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “He who does not show mercy to our young ones and does not recognize the rights of our elders is not from among us.”"
"273","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""He who does not show mercy to our young ones and does not respect our elders is not one of us."""
"274","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: Part of honoring Allah is to show respect to an elderly Muslim with white hair, to honor a carrier of the Qur'an who neither exaggerates in it nor neglects it, and to honor a just ruler."
"275","It is narrated from Rafi' bin Khadij and Sahl bin Abi Hathmah that both of them stated, or both narrated, that Abdullah bin Sahal and Muhayyisah bin Mas'ud both came to Khaybar and got separated from each other in an orchard. Then Abdullah bin Sahal was killed (while alone). So, Abdur Rahman bin Sahal and the two sons of Mas'ud, Huwayyisah and Muhayyisah, all three came together to the service of the Prophet (ﷺ) and began to talk about their (deceased) companion. Abdur Rahman began the conversation, and he was the youngest among them. So the Prophet (ﷺ) said to them, ""Let the elder begin."" Yahya says that (this means) the eldest should speak. So they spoke to the Prophet (ﷺ) about their companion's matter. The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""You can claim the right to the blood money of your slain companion by the oath of fifty men from your side."" (That is, fifty men should swear that the Jews killed him.) They said, ""O Messenger of Allah! This is something we did not witness. The Jews will be acquitted before you by swearing fifty oaths."" They said, ""O Messenger of Allah! These people are disbelievers. How can we accept their oaths?"" Upon this, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) paid the blood money himself. Sahl narrates: In this, a she-camel came to my share. I went to their enclosure, and it kicked me."
"276","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), he stated: Once the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Tell me about a tree which is like the example of a Muslim, which gives fruit by the command of its Lord in every season, its leaves do not fall, and it does not hide its fruit within its leaves?” In my heart, I thought that such a tree is the date palm tree, but I did not like to speak. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) were also present there. When both of them did not speak, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “It is the date palm tree.” When I left from there with my father, I said: Father! In my heart, I thought that it is the date palm tree. He said: Who stopped you from speaking? If you had said it, it would have been dearer to me than such and such things. I said: Since you and Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with them both) did not speak, I did not find it appropriate to speak."
"277","Hakeem bin Qais bin Asim narrated that his father (i.e., Qais bin Asim) advised his children at the time of his death, saying: Fear Allah, and appoint the eldest among you as your leader. When the people of a community appoint their elder as their leader, he acts as a deputy for their father. But when they appoint the younger as their leader, this is considered blameworthy among their peers. Make earning wealth and mastering its skills essential for yourselves. This is a cause of honor and fame for a noble person, and through this wealth, one can avoid dependence on a lowly person. Avoid asking from people; this is the lowest form of earning for a person (it is the last resort for sustenance). When I die, do not wail over me. Lamentation was not done at the death of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). When I die, bury me in any land, and do not let Bakr bin Wa'il know about my burial, because I used to ignore them during the days of ignorance."
"278","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: When nearly ripe dates (doke) were brought to the service of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he would supplicate: ""O Allah! Bless our Madinah, our mudd, and our sa', bless upon blessing."" After that, he would give the dates to the youngest child near him."
"279","Ya’la bin Murrah narrates that we went out with the Prophet (ﷺ). We were invited to a meal, and on the way, Sayyiduna Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him) was playing. The Prophet (ﷺ) hurried forward and stretched out his hands. Sometimes he (ﷺ) would pass from this side and sometimes from that side, making him (Husayn) laugh, until he (ﷺ) caught him. He (ﷺ) placed one hand under his chin and the other on his head, embraced him, and kissed him. Then the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Husayn is from me and I am from Husayn. May Allah love the one who loves Hasan and Husayn. They are two leaders among the leaders of the nations.”"
"280","Bukair narrates that he saw Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Ja'far (may Allah be pleased with him) kiss Zainab, the daughter of Umar bin Abu Salamah. At that time, Zainab was two years old or around that age."
"281","It is narrated from Hasan (al-Basri) that he said: If possible, do not even look at the hair of any woman in your household, except if she is your wife or a small girl, then you may do so."
"282","Yusuf bin Abdullah bin Salam says that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) named me Yusuf, seated me in his lap, and passed his hand over my head."
"283","It is narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she stated that I used to play with dolls in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). I had some friends who used to play with me, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would come, they would hide from him. He (peace and blessings be upon him) would send them to me, and then they would play with me."
"284","It is narrated from Abu Ajlan Muharibi who said: I was in the army of Abdullah bin Zubair. One of my paternal cousins passed away, and he had made a will to give a camel in the way of Allah. I said to his son, ""Give me the endowed camel because I am part of Abdullah bin Zubair's army."" He said, ""Come with me to Abdullah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) so that we may ask him for a fatwa."" We went to Abdullah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both). He (the son) said to Ibn Umar: ""O Abu Abdur Rahman! My father has passed away, and he made a will to give one of his camels in the way of Allah. And this is my cousin, and he is part of Ibn Zubair's army. Should I give him this camel?"" Abdullah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: ""O my son! 'The way of Allah' refers to every good deed. If your father made a will to give his camel in the way of Allah, then when you see a group of Muslims fighting in jihad against a group of polytheists, give the camel to those Muslims. And this man and his companions are fighting in the way of the children of the nation (not in the way of Allah), to see which of them gains power."""
"285","Sayyiduna Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah the Exalted will not show mercy to him."
"286","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy; whoever does not forgive will not be forgiven; whoever does not pardon will not be pardoned; whoever does not accept repentance will not have his repentance accepted; and whoever does not protect himself from sin will not be protected."
"287","It is narrated from Qarah that he said: A man said to the Messenger (ﷺ), ""O Messenger of Allah! When I slaughter a goat, I feel compassion for it."" Or he said, ""I feel compassion if I slaughter a goat."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said twice, ""If you show mercy to the goat, Allah will show mercy to you."""
"288","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the truthful, the believed, Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: ""Mercy is only taken away from the wretched."""
"289","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, was the most compassionate of all people towards his family. There was an infant at the outskirts of Madinah, and the husband of his nursing mother was a blacksmith. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, used to visit this child. He would find that the blacksmith had burned izkhar (a type of grass), filling the whole house with smoke. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, would kiss the child and hold him close to his mouth (smelling him)."
"290","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and with him was a child. He would embrace his child, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you feel mercy towards him?"" He replied: ""Yes."" The Prophet said: ""As much as you show mercy to him, Allah shows even more mercy to you, and He is the Most Merciful of those who show mercy."""
"291","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A man was walking along the road when he felt extremely thirsty. He found a well, so he went down into it and drank water. When he came out, he saw a dog panting and licking the wet earth out of thirst. The man said, 'This dog is suffering from thirst just as I was.' So he went down into the well again, filled his shoe with water, held it in his mouth, and climbed up, then gave the dog water to drink. Allah appreciated this deed of his and forgave him."" The people asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! Is there a reward for us in (doing good to) animals as well?"" He replied, ""There is a reward for (doing good to) every living being."""
"292","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A woman was punished because of a cat which she had tied up, until it died of hunger and thirst. She entered Hell because of that cat. It will be said to her (and Allah knows best): When you kept it tied up, you neither fed it nor gave it water, nor did you let it go free so that it could eat the insects of the earth."""
"293","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Show mercy, you will be shown mercy. Forgive, Allah will forgive you. Destruction is for those who hear something and ignore it, destruction is for those who persist in sins, those who stubbornly persist in their committed sins even though they know that it is unlawful."""
"294","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever shows mercy to anyone, even to an animal to be slaughtered, Allah will show mercy to him on the Day of Resurrection."""
"295","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah (ibn Mas'ud) (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped at a certain place, a man took some eggs from a wild bird. The bird came fluttering over the blessed head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Who among you has caused it distress by taking its eggs?"" A man said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I took its eggs."" He said: ""Have mercy on it and put the eggs back where they were."""
"296","It is narrated from Hisham bin Urwah that he said: When Ibn Zubair was in Makkah, the companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) used to carry birds in cages."
"297","Humaid bin Abdur Rahman reports that his mother, Umm Kulthum, who was the daughter of Uqbah bin Abi Mu’it, narrated that she heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “He is not a liar who reconciles between people, so (for reconciliation) he says something good or conveys something good.” She said: “I did not hear the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) permit lying to people except in three cases: for reconciling between people, a man speaking to his wife, and a woman speaking to her husband.” (That is, if a misunderstanding arises, something may be said for reconciliation whose apparent and inner meanings differ, but outright lying should still not be done.)"
"298","Sayyiduna Abdullah (ibn Mas'ud) (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Always remain steadfast upon truth, for indeed truthfulness leads to righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise. And indeed, a person continues to speak the truth until he is written with Allah as a truthful one (Siddiq). And always avoid lying, for indeed lying leads to wickedness (sins), and wickedness leads to Hell. A person continues to lie until he is written with Allah as a liar (Kadhdhab)."""
"299","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah (ibn Mas'ud) (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: Lying is not permissible, neither in seriousness nor in jest, nor in a situation where someone makes a promise to his child and then does not fulfill it."
"300","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""The believer who mixes with people and is patient over their harm is better than the one who does not mix with people and is not patient over their harm."""
"301","Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""No person or anything is more patient over something hurtful that he hears than Allah, the Mighty and Majestic. People claim that He has a child, yet He grants them well-being and provides them with sustenance."""
"302","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah (Ibn Mas'ud) (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed something, just as he used to distribute, upon which an Ansari said: ""By Allah! This is a distribution by which the pleasure of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, is not intended."" I said: ""I will surely inform the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of this."" So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was sitting among his companions, and I quietly told him this. This was very hard upon him. The color of his face changed, and he became angry, to the extent that I wished I had not said it. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Musa (peace be upon him) was harmed with more than this, but he was patient."""
"303","Sayyiduna Abu Darda narrates from the Prophet (ﷺ) that he (ﷺ) said: ""Shall I not tell you of something even better in rank than prayer, fasting, and charity?"" The people said, ""Certainly."" He (ﷺ) said: ""Reconciling between people, and on the contrary, spreading discord among people—this (habit) shaves off (faith)."""
"304","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said regarding the Qur’anic verse « فَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ وَأَصْلِحُوا ذَاتَ بَيْنِكُمْ » “Fear Allah and make reconciliation among yourselves”: This is a command from Allah that is obligatory upon the believers, that they should fear Allah and make reconciliation among themselves."
"305","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""My Ummah will not abandon two things: wailing (over the dead) and casting aspersions on lineage."""
"306","‘Awf bin Harith bin Tufail, who was the son of the stepbrother of Lady ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), narrates from Lady ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that once, Sayyiduna ‘Abdullah bin Zubair said regarding some purchase, sale, or gift of ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her): “By Allah! Either ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) refrains from this, or I will put a restriction on her.” (When this statement reached Lady ‘A’ishah [may Allah be pleased with her]), she said: “Did ‘Abdullah bin Zubair say this?” The people said: “Yes.” Upon this, ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: “(I) vow to Allah that I will never speak to Ibn Zubair again.” When the boycott of ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) from Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) became prolonged, he sought intercession from the Muhajirun. ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: “By Allah, I will not accept anyone’s intercession regarding him, and the vow I have made, I will never break it.” When this period became long for ‘Abdullah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him), he spoke to Miswar bin Makhramah and ‘Abdur Rahman bin Miswar bin ‘Abd Yaghuth, both of whom were from Banu Zuhrah, and said to them: “I beseech you both by Allah, take me to ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her). It is not permissible for her to take a vow to cut ties with me.” So Miswar and ‘Abdur Rahman took him along, and they had wrapped themselves in their cloaks. When they sought permission from ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), they said: “Peace be upon you and the mercy and blessings of Allah. May we come in?” ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) replied: “Yes, all of you come in.” They said: “O Mother of the Believers, shall we all come in?” She said: “Yes, all of you come in.” ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) did not know that ‘Abdullah bin Zubair was with them. When they entered, ‘Abdullah bin Zubair slipped inside the curtain. He embraced ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), pleaded with her, and began to weep, and Miswar and ‘Abdur Rahman also pleaded with ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) to speak to him and accept his apology, saying: “You know that the Messenger of Allah forbade boycotting, as you are aware. And it is not permissible for a man to continue a boycott with his brother for more than three days.” When they increased their advice and pressure, she would remind them of her oath and vow and would weep, saying: “I have made a very firm vow.” They continued to press her until she spoke to Ibn Zubair. Then, as expiation for her vow, she freed forty slaves. Even after freeing forty slaves, whenever she remembered this incident, she would weep until her scarf became wet with her tears. Upon this, Ibn Zubair spoke to Miswar bin Makhramah and ‘Abdur Rahman bin ‘Abd Yaghuth, both of whom were from Banu Zuhrah, and said to them: “I beseech you both by Allah, go to ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her). It is not permissible for her to take a vow to cut ties with me.” Miswar and ‘Abdur Rahman hid ‘Abdullah bin Zubair in their cloak and reached there, and sought permission from ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) to enter, saying: “Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy and blessings of Allah. May we come in?” Upon this, ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: “You all come in.” They both said again: “Shall we all come in?” She said: “Yes, all of you come in.” ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) was not aware that Ibn Zubair was with them. When all of them entered, Ibn Zubair went inside the curtain and, placing his head on the shoulder of ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), began to plead and weep, and from outside the curtain, Miswar and ‘Abdur Rahman insisted to ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) to accept his excuse and speak to him. Both of them began to say: “You know well that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) has forbidden cutting off relations, and it is not permissible for any person to cut off relations with his Muslim brother for more than three nights.” ‘Awf narrated that when they advised her a lot and troubled her, she began to understand and started to weep, saying: “I have made a vow, and the vow is severe.” They continued to plead until she spoke to ‘Abdullah bin Zubair, and then, as expiation for her vow, she freed forty souls. After that, even when she had freed forty souls, whenever she mentioned it, her tears would wet her scarf."
"307","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Do not bear malice against one another, do not envy one another, do not boycott one another, and O servants of Allah! Be brothers to one another. It is not lawful for any Muslim to boycott his Muslim brother for more than three days. Do not speak ill behind each other's backs, and O servants of Allah, live as brothers among yourselves. It is not lawful for any Muslim to sever relations with his brother for more than three nights.”"
"308","It is narrated from the companion of the Messenger of Allah, Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for a person to boycott his brother for more than three days. When they meet, both turn away from each other, and the better of the two is the one who greets first."""
"309","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Do not harbor hatred among yourselves, do not envy one another, and do not act with hypocrisy. Be, O servants of Allah, brothers to one another."""
"310","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When two persons love each other for the sake of Allah, or he said, for the sake of Islam, then the first sin committed by either of them causes separation between them."""
"311","It is narrated from Hisham bin 'Amir Ansari, who was a cousin of Anas bin Malik and whose father was martyred on the day of Uhud, that he said he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""It is not permissible for a Muslim to cut off relations with another Muslim for more than three days. As long as both of them persist in this estrangement, they remain away from the truth. And whoever reconciles first, his initiative will be an expiation for his sin. If they die in this state of estrangement, they will never enter Paradise together. And if one of them greets the other and the other does not accept his greeting, then an angel responds to the one who greeted, and Satan responds to the one who refused. Whoever ends this situation first, his action will be an expiation for the previous mistake. And if both die in this state, neither of them will ever enter Paradise. And if one greets and the other refuses to accept the greeting, then an angel responds to the one who greeted, and Satan responds to the one who refused."""
"312","Narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I know when you are angry and when you are pleased."" I asked, ""How do you know that?"" He said: ""Indeed, when you are happy, you say (when swearing an oath), 'Yes, by the Lord of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him),' and when you are angry, you say, 'Yes, by the Lord of Ibrahim.'"" Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I replied, ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah, it is just as you say. I only avoid mentioning your name."""
"313","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Khirash Salmi, may Allah be pleased with him, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say: ""Whoever severs ties with his brother for a year, it is as if he has shed his blood (i.e., killed him)."""
"314","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for a Muslim to sever relations with his brother for more than three days; when they meet, one turns away from the other and the other turns away from him. The better of the two is the one who greets (with salam) first."""
"315","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not bear malice against one another, do not envy one another, and be, O servants of Allah, brothers to one another."""
"316","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, the worst person in the sight of Allah will be the two-faced person who comes to some people with one face and to others with another face. He comes to these people with one side and to those people with the other side."""
"317","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Always avoid suspicion, for suspicion is the most false of speech, and do not artificially raise prices to entrap others, do not quarrel with one another, do not envy one another, do not harbor malice against one another, do not give preference to yourselves with hypocrisy or enmity, do not sever relations with one another, and O servants of Allah, become brothers to one another."""
"318","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The gates of Paradise are opened on Mondays and Thursdays, and every servant who does not associate anything with Allah is forgiven, except for the person between whom and his brother there is enmity. It is said regarding them: Give them respite until they reconcile with each other."""
"319","Sayyiduna Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Shall I not tell you a hadith that is better for you than charity and fasting? (That thing is) reconciling between two who are fighting. Beware! Indeed, sowing enmity between them is something that shaves (destroys)."
"320","It is narrated from Wahb bin Kaysan, who lived during the time of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), he says: Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) saw a shepherd and goats grazing in a barren (ruined place), and he also saw a better place, so he said, ""May Allah reward you, O shepherd! Drive the goats (to the better place). I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say that every shepherd is responsible (answerable) for his flock."""
"321","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""An evil example is not for us (it does not befit us); the one who gives something as a gift and then takes it back is like a dog that licks up its own vomit."""
"322","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A believer is simple and generous, and a wicked person is deceitful and miserly."""
"323","It is narrated from Umm Darda (and she is the younger Umm Darda who was a scholar), that a man came to her and said: A person has spoken ill of you in the presence of Abdul Malik. She replied: If he has said something about us which is not in us, then for a long time virtues have been attributed to us which were not in us. (Abu Darda had two wives; when the first wife passed away, he married again, and she is called the younger Umm Darda.)"
"324","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah (Ibn Mas'ud): When a person says to his companion, ""You are my enemy,"" then one of them goes out of Islam, or (if he says), ""I am free from responsibility towards my companion."""
"325","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), and Tawus says: I think he narrated it as marfu’ (attributed) to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). Laith is in doubt. He said: The son of Adam has three hundred and sixty joints, or bones or joints, and on each of them charity is due every day. Every good word is a charity, a man’s helping his brother is charity, and giving a drink of water is charity, and removing something harmful from the road is also charity. « الشَّرْبَةُ :» Fulfilling the need of providing a complete drink of water in a gathering."
"326","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""When two people abuse each other, the sin is upon the one who started it, as long as the oppressed (the one who was abused first) does not exceed the limits."""
"327","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""When two people exchange insults, the sin is upon the one who started it, as long as the wronged one does not exceed the limits."""
"328","And the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Do you know what «عضه» (slander) is?"" The people replied: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: ""It is conveying a statement from one person to another so that discord arises among them."""
"329","And the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has revealed to me that you should adopt humility, and that none of you should wrong another."""
"330","Iyad bin Hamar said that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Indeed, Allah has revealed to me that you should adopt humility, so that no one oppresses another and no one boasts over another.” Upon this I said: O Messenger of Allah, if someone abuses me in a large gathering and he is of a lower status than me, and I respond to him, will I also be sinful for that? He said: “Two people who abuse each other are both devils, who utter foul words and lie.”"
"331","Iyad says: I used to defend the Prophet (ﷺ), so I sent him a she-camel as a gift before I became Muslim. The Prophet (ﷺ) did not accept it and said: ""I dislike the gifts of the polytheists."""
"332","Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: “Abusing a Muslim is wickedness. (If a person, while being a Muslim, utters abuse from his mouth, this is a sin.)”"
"333","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was neither foul-mouthed nor did he curse, nor did he use abusive language. When he became angry, he would say: ""What is the matter with him, may his forehead be covered with dust."""
"334","Sayyiduna Abdullah (bin Mas'ud) narrates from the Prophet (ﷺ): ""Abusing a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief."""
"335","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""No man should accuse another man of being a sinner, nor issue a verdict of disbelief against him. If his companion is not deserving of it, then that verdict returns upon the one who uttered it."""
"336","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever knowingly claims to be the son of someone other than his father has committed disbelief, and whoever claims to belong to a people to whom he does not belong, he should take his place in Hell. And whoever calls someone a disbeliever or says 'enemy of Allah' to someone who is not so, this will return upon the one who said it."""
"337","Adi bin Thabit says that I heard Sulaiman bin Surad, a companion of the Prophet (ﷺ), say: Two persons abused each other in the presence of the Prophet (ﷺ). One of them became so angry that his face swelled and his color changed. Upon this, the Prophet (ﷺ) said: I know a sentence, if he were to say it, what he is experiencing would go away. A man went to him and informed him of what the Prophet (ﷺ) had said and told him: Say «اعوذ بالله من الشيطان الرجيم» . He replied: Do you think I am sick or mad? Go mind your own business."
"338","It is narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did an act and granted a concession in it. A group of people abstained from it. When this matter reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he delivered a sermon, praised Allah, and then said: ""What is the matter with some people? They abstain from participating in the act which I have done. By Allah, I know Allah better than them and I fear Him more than they do."""
"339","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me and Zubair bin Al-Awwam, and both of us were horsemen. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Go until you reach such-and-such garden. There you will find a woman. She has a letter which Hatib has written to the polytheists. Bring that letter to me."" We found that woman on her camel at exactly the place the Prophet (peace be upon him) had indicated for us. So we said to her: ""Where is the letter that is with you?"" She said: ""I have no letter."" So we searched her and her camel. My companion said: ""I think she does not have it."" I said: ""By the One in Whose hand is my soul, the Prophet (peace be upon him) has never spoken falsely. O woman, either produce the letter or I will strip you naked."" So she lowered her hand to her back. She was wearing a woolen waistband. From it, she took out the letter. We brought the letter to the Prophet (peace be upon him). Upon this, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""This man (Hatib) has betrayed Allah, His Messenger (peace be upon him), and all the Muslims. Allow me to strike off his head."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said (to Hatib): ""What made you do this?"" He said: ""What happened to me except that I am a believer in Allah? My intention was that I would have a favor with those people (the people of Makkah)."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""O Umar! He has spoken the truth. Is he not among those who fought at Badr? Perhaps Allah has looked at them and said: 'Do whatever you wish, Paradise has been made obligatory for you.'"" So tears began to flow from both eyes of Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), and he said: ""Allah and His Messenger (peace be upon him) know best."""
"340","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever calls his brother a disbeliever, then surely one of them will return with disbelief."""
"341","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a person calls another a disbeliever, then one of them has certainly committed disbelief. If the one who was called a disbeliever is truly so, then the accuser has spoken the truth. But if he is not as he was described, then the one who uttered the word of disbelief will himself return with disbelief."""
"342","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge from the evil of fate's decrees and from the enemies rejoicing over him. (No decision of Allah is bad; the evil here is due to the person himself. Sometimes the decrees of fate become difficult for a person.)"
"343","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Allah is pleased with three things for you and displeased with three things. He likes for you that you worship Him, do not associate anything with Him, and all of you hold fast to the rope of Allah together, and that you show goodwill to those whom Allah has placed in authority over you (i.e., the rulers). And He dislikes for you idle talk, excessive questioning, and wasting wealth.” (There are three meanings of questioning: one should not ask too many questions regarding religious rulings, should not beg from people, and should not ask people personal questions.)"
"344","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding the saying of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: « وَمَا أَنْفَقْتُمْ مِنْ شَيْءٍ فَهُوَ يَخْلُفُهُ وَهُوَ خَيْرُ الرَّازِقِينَ ‏» ""And whatever you spend, Allah will replace it, and He is the best of providers."" In its explanation, it is reported that this is except for extravagance and miserliness."
"345","It is narrated from Abu Al-‘Ubaydeen, he says: I asked Abdullah ibn Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) about «مبذرين» , so he said: These are the people who spend extravagantly."
"346","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): He said about «مبذرين» who spend without right."
"347","It is narrated from Aslam that Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say from the pulpit: O people, put your houses in order and scare away these snakes before they scare you. Surely, their being Muslims will never be apparent to you, and by Allah! Since we have become hostile to them, we have never reconciled with them."
"348","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Khabbab (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: Indeed, a person is rewarded for spending wealth in everything except for building (constructing) a house."
"349","It is narrated from Nafi' bin Asim that he heard Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) say to his nephew: ""Those who had come out from the lower part (the pit), are your laborers working?"" He replied: ""I do not know."" He said: ""If you were from Banu Thaqif, you would do exactly what your laborers are doing."" After that, he turned to us and said: ""When a man works himself in his house along with his laborers,"" and (the narrator) Abu Asim once said: ""works in his wealth,"" then he is one of the agents of Allah, the Exalted."
"350","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not come until people compete with one another in constructing tall buildings."""
"351","Hasan (al-Basri) says that during the caliphate of Sayyiduna Uthman ibn Affan (may Allah be pleased with him), I used to go to the houses of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and I would touch their roofs with my hands."
"352","Dawud bin Qais narrated that I saw the (rooms of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ); they were made of palm branches. From the outside, they were covered with hair-cloth mats, and I think that the width of the house from the door of the room to the door of the house was six or seven handspans. And I estimated the inner part of the house; its length from inside was ten handspans, and the height was between seven and eight handspans, or close to that. I stood at the door of Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her); this door was towards the west."
"353","It is narrated from Qais bin Abi Hazim, he said that we went to visit Khabbab. He had been cauterized seven times. He said, ""Indeed, our predecessors have passed away and the world could not diminish their status in the least, and indeed we have acquired so much that now we find no place to spend it except in the earth (i.e., burying it). And if the Prophet (peace be upon him) had not forbidden praying for death, I would have prayed for death."" After that, when we came again, we saw that he was building one of his walls. He said, ""A Muslim receives reward for all his expenses except for what he spends in the earth (i.e., on building a house)."""
"354","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with him, who says that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, passed by while I was repairing my room. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, asked: ""What are you doing?"" I said: O Messenger of Allah! I am repairing my room. He said: ""The matter is even more urgent than this"" (meaning death can come even more swiftly than this)."
"355","Sayyiduna Nafi’ bin ‘Abd al-Harith (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: “Among the good fortune of a person is a spacious house, a righteous neighbor, and a comfortable ride.”"
"356","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until people start building houses that they decorate and make resemble saddles (with adornments)."" Ibrahim said: That is, striped cloth."
"357","It is narrated from Warad, who was the scribe of Mughira, that he said: (Once) Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote to Mughira: ""Write to me something that you have heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)."" So Mughira (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote to him: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to recite this supplication after every prayer: « لاَ إِلَهَ إِلاَّ اللَّهُ وَحْدَهُ لاَ شَرِيكَ لَهُ ، لَهُ الْمُلْكُ وَلَهُ الْحَمْدُ ، وَهُوَ عَلَى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ ، اللَّهُمَّ لاَ مَانِعَ لِمَا أَعْطَيْتَ ، وَلاَ مُعْطِيَ لَمَا مَنَعْتَ ، وَلاَ يَنْفَعُ ذَا الْجَدِّ مِنْكَ الْجَدُّ .» ""There is no deity except Allah, He is One, He has no partner, His is the dominion and to Him belongs all praise, and He is over all things competent. O Allah! None can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the wealth of the wealthy will not avail them against You."" And he also wrote to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade idle talk, excessive questioning, and the wasting of wealth. And he (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade disobedience to mothers, burying daughters alive, withholding the rights of people, and asking without right."
"358","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No one's deeds can save him."" The people asked: ""Not even you, O Messenger of Allah?"" He replied: ""Not even me, unless Allah covers me with His mercy. Therefore, remain steadfast, draw close to one another, and perform good deeds in the morning, in the evening, and to some extent during the latter part of the night. And adopt moderation, adopt moderation, and you will reach your destination."""
"359","Narrated from Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), she says: Once a group of Jews came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: « السَّامُ عَلَيْكُمْ » ""Destruction be upon you."" Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says: I understood, so I said: « عَلَيْكُمُ السَّامُ وَاللَّعْنَةُ » She says: Upon this, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Wait, O Aisha! Indeed, Allah loves gentleness in all matters."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Did you not hear what they said?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have already said: ' « وَعَلَيْكُمْ » and the same be upon you.'"""
"360","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jarir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever is deprived of gentleness is deprived of all kinds of goodness."""
"361","Sayyiduna Abu Darda’ (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: “Whoever has been given his share of gentleness has been given his share of goodness, and whoever is deprived of his share of gentleness has been deprived of his share of goodness. On the Day of Resurrection, the heaviest thing in the believer’s scale will be good character, and indeed Allah dislikes the foul-mouthed, ill-mannered person.”"
"362","It is narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Forgive the mistakes of those who have good character (righteous people)."""
"363","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""Harshness makes anything in which it is found ugly. Indeed, Allah is gentle and loves gentleness."""
"364","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, was more modest than a veiled virgin girl. When something displeased him, we would recognize it from his face."
"365","Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that I was riding a camel that was unruly (stubborn), the camel was a bit harsh. Upon this, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Always adopt gentleness. This quality adorns whatever it is found in, and whatever it is removed from, it makes it defective."""
"366","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of miserliness, for indeed it destroyed those before you. They shed each other's blood and severed their ties of kinship, and oppression will be many darknesses on the Day of Resurrection. And beware of foul speech. Indeed, Allah does not like the one who is obscene in speech and deliberately abusive."""
"367","Kathir bin Ubaid says: I came to Umm al-Mu’minin Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), and she said: Hold this for me so I can sew my trousers. So I held it. I said: O Umm al-Mu’minin, if I go outside and mention this matter to people, they will consider it stinginess on your part. She said: Do your work; new clothes are not for the one who does not use the old."
"368","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mughaffal (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Indeed, Allah is gentle. He loves gentleness, and He gives for gentleness what He does not give for harshness."""
"369","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Make things easy, do not make them difficult, give comfort to the hearts, do not cause aversion."""
"370","It is narrated from Harith bin Laqit, he said: When a mare of any one of us would give birth, he would kill it and say: Will I live until I can ride it? Then a letter from Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) came to us, stating: Take good care of whatever Allah has given you. Indeed, there is ease in this matter."
"371","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that if the Day of Judgment comes while you have a date-palm sapling in your hand, and if you are able to plant it before the Hour is established, then you should certainly plant it."
"372","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""Three supplications are accepted: the supplication of the oppressed, the supplication of the traveler, and the supplication of a father against his children."""
"373","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Beware of oppression, for oppression will be darkness upon darkness on the Day of Resurrection. And beware of miserliness, for miserliness destroyed those before you. It led them to shed each other's blood and to make lawful what was forbidden to them."""
"374","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Oppression will be many darknesses on the Day of Resurrection."""
"375","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""When the people of faith are saved from Hell (the Bridge of Sirat), they will be stopped on a bridge between Paradise and Hell, and they will settle the wrongs they committed against each other in the world. And when they are purified and cleansed, then they will be allowed to enter Paradise. So, by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), each of them will recognize his dwelling in Paradise better than he recognized it in the world."""
"376","Abu Wada'hi narrates that Masruq and Shatir bin Shakl gathered together in the mosque, so all the circles in the mosque converged towards them. Upon this, Masruq said, ""I think these people have gathered around us only to hear something good. Either you narrate from Abdullah and I will confirm, or I will narrate from Abdullah and you confirm."" He said, ""O Abu Aishah, you narrate."" He said, ""Have you heard Abdullah bin Mas'ud say that the eyes commit adultery, the hands commit adultery, the feet commit adultery, and the private part either confirms or denies it?"" He said, ""Yes (I have heard it)."" He said, ""I have also heard it."" He said, ""Have you also heard from Abdullah that there is no verse in the Noble Qur'an greater than this verse in which all lawful and unlawful, commands and prohibitions have been mentioned? That verse is: «إن الله يأمر بالعدل والإحسان وإيتاء ذي القربى» 'Indeed, Allah commands justice and good conduct and giving to relatives.'"" He said, ""Yes."" He said, ""I have also heard it."" He said, ""Have you also heard from Abdullah that there is no verse in the Noble Qur'an that removes people's difficulties more quickly than this verse: «ومن يتق الله يجعل له مخرجا» 'And whoever fears Allah, He will make for him a way out.'"" He said, ""Yes."" He said, ""I have also heard it."" He said, ""Have you also heard from Abdullah that there is no verse in the Noble Qur'an in which there is greater reliance (submission) than this: «يا عبادي الذين أسرفوا على أنفسهم لا تقنطوا» 'O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah.'"" He said, ""Yes."" He said, ""I have also heard it."""
"377","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he narrates from Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, that Allah said: ""O My servants! Indeed, I have made oppression unlawful for Myself and I have made it unlawful for you as well, so do not oppress one another. O My servants! You commit sins day and night, and I am the One who forgives all sins, and it does not concern Me. Seek forgiveness from Me, I will forgive you. O My servants! All of you are hungry except those whom I feed, so ask Me for food, I will feed you. O My servants! All of you are unclothed except those whom I clothe, so ask Me for clothing, I will clothe you. O My servants! If the first and the last of you, and all humans and jinn among you, were to become as pious as the most pious heart among you, that would not increase My dominion in the least. And if the most wicked heart among you were to become as wicked as possible, that would not decrease My dominion in the least. If all of you were to gather in one plain and ask Me, and I were to give every person what he asked for, that would not decrease what I possess any more than a needle decreases the sea when dipped into it once. O My servants! These are your deeds which I account for you. So whoever finds good, let him praise Allah, and whoever finds otherwise, let him blame no one but himself."" (Imam Shafi'i) Whenever Abu Idris narrated this hadith, he would rest both his knees on the ground."
"378","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri and Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with them) narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""When any Muslim experiences fatigue, illness, anxiety, sorrow, pain, or grief—even to the extent that a thorn pricks him—then Allah, because of that, removes his sins."""
"379","It is narrated from Sa'id that he said: I was with Salman when he visited a sick person from the Kindah tribe. When Salman came to the patient, he said: ""Glad tidings! Indeed, Allah makes the illness of a believer an expiation (for sins) and a cause of (His) pleasure. And the illness of a wicked person is like when the people of a household tie up a camel and then release it. It does not know why it was tied up or why it was released."""
"380","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""A believing man or woman continues to be tested in his body, his family, and his wealth, until he meets Allah in such a state that there remains no sin upon him."""
"381","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a Bedouin came, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Has Umm Mildam ever seized you?"" He said: What is Umm Mildam? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is heat between the skin and the flesh."" (i.e., fever). He said: Never. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Have you ever had a headache (suda‘)?"" He said: What is suda‘? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is a wind that enters the head and strikes the veins."" (i.e., headache). He said: Never. Then when he stood up, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever wishes to look at a man from the people of Hell, let him look at this one."""
"382","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""When a believer falls ill, Allah purifies him (from sins) just as a furnace purifies iron from rust."""
"383","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""When a Muslim is afflicted with pain or illness, even if a thorn pricks him or he suffers any hardship, it becomes an expiation for his sins."""
"384","Sa’d’s daughter Aisha narrates that my father said: I once became seriously ill in Mecca. The Prophet (ﷺ) came to visit me, so I said, “O Messenger of Allah! I am leaving behind wealth and I have only one daughter. Should I bequeath two-thirds of my wealth and leave one-third?” He said, “No.” I asked, “Should I bequeath half and leave half for my daughter?” He said, “No.” I asked, “Then should I bequeath one-third and leave two-thirds for my daughter?” He said, “Yes, one-third, and one-third is a lot.” After that, he placed his hand on my forehead, passed it over my face and stomach, and then prayed, “O Allah! Grant Sa’d healing and complete his migration.” Since then, to this day, whenever I remember, I feel the coolness of your blessed hand on my liver."
"385","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""When a person falls ill, the deeds that he used to do in a state of health are written for him."""
"386","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that whenever Allah Almighty puts a person to a physical trial, then as long as he remains ill, the same deeds are written for him as he used to do in a state of health. If Allah grants the patient recovery, I think the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""His sins are washed away, and if Allah takes him (in death), He forgives him."" And in another narration: ""If Allah grants him recovery, He washes him clean of sins."""
"387","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: Fever came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: ""Send me to those among your people who have more precedence."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sent it to the Ansar. It remained with them for six days and nights, and the fever proved to be very severe for them. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came to their houses, and the people complained to him. Upon this, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) began to visit each neighborhood and each house of theirs and started praying for their well-being. When he was returning, a woman came behind him and said: ""By the One Who has sent you with the truth, I am from the Ansar and my father is also from the Ansar. Just as you prayed for the Ansar, pray for me as well."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What do you want? If you wish, I will pray for you to be protected from fever, and if you wish, be patient and you will be granted Paradise."" She said: ""I will be patient, and I will not put Paradise at risk."""
"388","Ata narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: ""There is no illness more beloved to me than fever; fever enters into every part of my body, and Allah grants every part its share of reward."""
"389","It is narrated from Abu Nahilah that it was said to him: Pray to Allah, so he said: O Allah! Lessen the illness but do not decrease the reward. Then it was said to him: Pray, and when he prayed, he said: O Allah! Make me among the close ones and make my mother among the houris with beautiful eyes."
"390","It is narrated from Ata bin Abi Rabah that Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) said to me: ""Shall I not show you a woman of Paradise?"" I said: ""Certainly."" He said: ""This black woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: 'I have fits of epilepsy and I become uncovered, so please pray to Allah for me.' The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'If you wish, be patient and Paradise will be yours, or if you wish, I will pray to Allah to cure you.' The woman said: 'I will be patient, but I become uncovered, so please pray to Allah that I may not become uncovered.' So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed for her."""
"391","It is narrated from Ata that he saw a tall black woman, Umm Zafar, on the steps of the Ka'bah. It is narrated from Qasim that Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say that when a believer is pricked by a thorn or suffers anything greater (or lesser) than that, it becomes an expiation for him."
"392","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If a thorn pricks any Muslim in this world and he remains patient, then on the Day of Resurrection, in exchange for that, some sin of his will be forgiven."""
"393","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whenever a believing man or a believing woman, or a Muslim man or a Muslim woman, is afflicted with any illness, Allah, in return, forgives their sins."""
"394","Hisham narrates from his father that he said: I and Abdullah bin Zubair went to Lady Asma’ (may Allah be pleased with her) ten days before Abdullah (bin Zubair) was killed, and Lady Asma’ (may Allah be pleased with her) was ill. Abdullah said to her: How are you feeling? She said: I am in pain. Abdullah said: Death is facing me (my death is certain). Asma’ (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Perhaps you want me to die, so you wish for it. Do not do so. By Allah! I do not wish for death until your matter is decided, either you are killed and I will be patient over it, or you are victorious and my eyes will be cooled. Beware, do not agree to any suggestion out of fear of death with which you are not satisfied. Abdullah had in his heart that he would be killed, so Asma’ (may Allah be pleased with her), his mother, would not have to bear the shock."
"395","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) that he once came to the service of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and at that time you had a severe fever. You had a sheet over you, and he placed his hand on top of the sheet and felt the heat of the fever through the sheet. So Abu Sa'id said: ""O Messenger of Allah! How intense is your fever!"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Just as the trial upon us is very severe, likewise the reward for us is also doubled."" Upon this (Abu Sa'id) said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Which people are tested the most?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The Prophets, then the righteous. And among them, a man is tested with poverty until he has nothing except a long cloak, which he tears at the collar and wears, and he is afflicted with lice until (the lice) kill him. And these people would be as happy with trials as one of you is not even with a gift."""
"396","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that (once) I fell ill, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) came to visit me on foot. They found me in a state of unconsciousness, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and poured the leftover water of his ablution over me, and I regained consciousness. I saw that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was present, so I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! What should I decide regarding my wealth? How should I decide about my wealth?"" He did not give me any answer until the verse of inheritance was revealed."
"397","Narrated from Sayyiduna Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) that the child of the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became very seriously ill, so his mother sent a message to the Prophet (peace be upon him) that my son is at the throes of death. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said to the messenger: ""Go and say to her: «إن لله ما أخذ ، وله ما أعطى ، وكل شيء عنده إلى أجل مسمى ، فلتصبر ولتحتسب .» 'To Allah belongs what He takes and to Him belongs what He gives, and everything with Him has an appointed term, so she should be patient and seek reward from Allah.'"" The messenger went back and conveyed your message to her. She sent another message to you and made you swear that you must come, so the Prophet (peace be upon him) got up with some of his companions, among whom was Sa’d bin ‘Ubadah. The Prophet (peace be upon him) took the child and placed him on his chest. The child’s chest was making sounds like the sound of water dripping from an old water skin. Tears flowed from the eyes of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). Sa’d said: Are you weeping, even though you are the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""I am only weeping out of mercy for him. Allah only shows mercy to His merciful servants."""
"398","Ibrahim bin Abi Ablah narrates that my wife fell ill. At that time, I used to visit Umm Darda. Whenever I went, she would ask me, ""How is your wife?"" I would reply, ""She is ill."" Then she would have food brought for me and I would eat. Then I went again and she did the same (gave me food). Then once I went to her and she asked, ""How is your wife?"" I said, ""She is recovering."" She said, ""When you used to tell us that your wife was ill, I would have food brought for you, but now that she is getting better, we will not have anything brought for you."""
"399","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) went to visit a Bedouin who was ill (it is said that the Prophet’s practice was that when he went to visit a sick person) he would say: «لا بأس عليك ، طهور إن شاء الله» “No harm, if Allah wills, it will be a purification from sins.” (Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said:) That Bedouin said (Is it a purification? Never!) Rather, this fever is raging against an old man so that it may take him to the graveyard. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Alright, then let it be as you say.”"
"400","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Who among you has fasted today?"" Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I have. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Who among you has visited a sick person today?"" Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I have. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Who among you has attended a funeral today?"" Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I have. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: ""Who has fed a poor person today?"" Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I have. Marwan said that I have learned that (upon this) the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When all these qualities are combined in a person in a single day, he will enter Paradise."""
"401","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Umm Sa’ib, and she was shivering due to fever. He asked: “What has happened to you?” She said: “It is fever, may Allah disgrace it.” Upon this, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Be quiet, do not speak ill of it. It removes the sins of a believer just as a furnace removes the rust from iron.”"
"402","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Allah says: I asked you for food and you did not feed Me. The servant will say, ‘O my Lord! How could I feed You, while You are the Lord of the worlds?’ Allah will say: Did you not know that My such-and-such servant asked you for food but you did not feed him? Did you not know that if you had fed him, you would have found its reward with Me? O son of Adam! I asked you for water and you did not give Me water to drink. He will say, ‘O my Lord! How could I give You water to drink, while You are the Lord of the worlds?’ Allah will say: My such-and-such servant asked you for water and you did not give him. Did you not know that if you had given him water to drink, you would have found its reward with Me? O son of Adam! I fell ill and you did not visit Me. The servant will say, ‘O my Lord! How could I visit You when You are the Lord of the worlds?’ Allah will say: Did you not know that My such-and-such servant fell ill, and if you had visited him, you would have found its reward with Me or found Me with him.”"
"403","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""Visit the sick, attend funerals, this will remind you of the Hereafter."""
"404","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""These three acts are the right of every Muslim: visiting the sick, attending the funeral, and responding to the one who sneezes if he says 'Alhamdulillah'."""
"405","The three sons of Sa’d narrated from their father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to visit Sa’d in Mecca when Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) began to weep. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: “Why are you weeping?” He said: I fear that I might die in this land from which I migrated, just as Sa’d (bin Khawlah) passed away. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said three times: “O Allah! Grant Sa’d healing.” Then Sa’d said: I have much wealth, and my only heir is my daughter. Should I bequeath all my wealth (in the way of Allah)? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “No.” He said: Two-thirds? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “No.” He said: Half of my wealth? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “No.” He said: Then a third of my wealth? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Yes, a third, and a third is still much. Whatever charity you give from your wealth is charity, and your spending on your wife and children is charity. And whatever your wife eats from your food is charity. And if you leave your family well-off or, he said, provided for, that is better than leaving them in a state where they have to stretch out their hands before people.” And he gestured with his hand."
"406","It is narrated from Abu Asma that he said: Whoever visits his brother (in illness) will be in a garden of Paradise. I asked Abu Qilabah: What is meant by a garden of Paradise? He replied: Its fruits. I asked Abu Qilabah: From whom did Abu Asma narrate this hadith? He said: From Thawban, and Thawban narrates from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him."
"407","It is narrated from Abu Bakr bin Hazm and Muhammad bin Munkadir that they were among some people of the mosque who visited Umar bin Hakam bin Rafi’ Al-Ansari during his illness. He said: O Abu Hafs! Tell us a hadith. He said: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) say: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Whoever visits a sick person enters into mercy, and when he sits there, he settles in an ocean of mercy.”"
"408","Ata reported that Umar bin Safwan visited me when I was ill. When the time for prayer came, Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) led them in two units of prayer and said: I am a traveler (therefore I shortened the prayer and performed half of it)."
"409","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that a Jewish boy used to serve the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). He fell ill, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came to visit him and sat by his head and said: ""Become a Muslim."" The boy looked towards his father, who was sitting by his head. The father said to him: ""Obey Abul Qasim."" So the boy became a Muslim. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) left from him saying, ""Praise be to Allah who saved him from the Fire."""
"410","Narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Madinah, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) became ill. She says: I went to them. I said: O my father! How are you? And O Bilal! How are you? When Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) would have a fever, he would say: Every man wakes up among his family, and death is closer to him than the strap of his sandal. And when Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) would recover from the fever, he would raise his voice and say: Oh, if only I could spend a night in a valley surrounded by the bushes of Idhkhir and Jalil, and will they ever intend to go to the springs of Majannah, and will there ever be a time when the hills of Shamah and Tufail will appear for me (they were remembering the places of Makkah). Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of their condition, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: «اللهم حبب إلينا المدينة، كحبنا مكة أو أشد، وصححها، وبارك لنا فى صاعها ومدها، وانقل حماها فاجعلها بالجحفة» ""O Allah! Make Madinah as beloved to us as Makkah or even more so, and make it healthy for us, and bless us in its sa’ and its mudd, and transfer its fever to the valley of Juhfa."""
"411","Sa'id bin 'Amr bin Sa'id narrates from his father that he said: Hajjaj came to Sayyiduna Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) while I was with him. He asked, ""How are you?"" He replied, ""I am fine."" He asked, ""Who wounded you?"" He replied, ""The one who ordered weapons to be raised on the day when raising weapons was not permissible,"" meaning Hajjaj wounded him (since he ordered his army to fight)."
"412","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Abi Huzail that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) went to visit a sick person. Some other people were with him, and there was also a woman in the house. One of the people began to look towards the woman, so Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: If your eye were to be blinded, it would be better for you."
"413","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Zaid bin Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) that my eye was hurting, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited me to inquire about my health."
"414","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said: When I test My servant by taking away his two beloved things, meaning his two eyes, and he remains patient, I give him Paradise in return."""
"415","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he reports from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Allah says: O son of Adam, when I take away your two most beloved things (your eyes), and you endure this calamity with patience and seek reward, then I will not be pleased with any reward for you less than Paradise."""
"416","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would visit a sick person, he would sit near his head and then say this seven times: «أسأل الله العظيم ، رب العرش العظيم أن يشفيك» ""I ask the Mighty Allah, Lord of the Great Throne, to grant you healing."" If the death of that patient was to be delayed, he would be freed from that affliction."
"417","Rabi' bin Abdullah narrates: I went with Hasan to visit Qatadah, so he (Hasan) sat near Qatadah's head, then asked about his condition and prayed for him, saying: O Allah! Grant healing to his heart and remove his illness."
"418","It is narrated from Aswad that he said: I asked Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), ""What did the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) do in his house?"" She said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to be engaged in the work of his family, and when the time for prayer came, he would go out."
"419","It is narrated from Urwah that I asked Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), ""What did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do in his house?"" She said: ""He used to mend his own shoes and did the same work that a man does in his house."" (And in another narration, she said: ""What does any one of you do in his house? He sews his shoes, patches his clothes, and stitches them."")"
"420","It is narrated from Umrah that Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) was asked: What did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) do in his house? She said: He was just like any other human being; he would dust and clean his clothes and milk his goat."
"421","It is narrated from Habib bin Ubaid, who narrates from Sayyiduna Miqdam bin Ma'dikarib (may Allah be pleased with him), and he also lived in his time. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When one of you loves his brother, he should inform him that he loves him."""
"422","It is narrated from Mujahid that he said: I met a man from among the companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him), who held my shoulders from behind and said: Listen, I love you. Mujahid said: May Allah also love you, for whose pleasure you have loved me. Upon this he said: If the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) had not said that when a person loves another person, he should inform him that he loves him, I would never have told you this. After that, he began to offer me a marriage proposal and said: Listen, we have a girl, but she is blind."
"423","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When two people love each other (for the sake of Allah), the better of them is the one who loves his companion more."""
"424","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: When you love your brother, do not quarrel with him, do not harm him, and do not inquire about him, for it is possible that you may meet one of his enemies who will say things about him that are not true, and thus create separation between you and him."
"425","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that he heard this statement at Siffin. He used to say: Intelligence is in the heart, mercy is in the liver, gentleness (compassion) is in the spleen, and breath is in the lungs."
"426","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) says that we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) when a man from among the Bedouins came. He was wearing a green shawl cloak. He came and stood over the head of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: ""Your companion has lowered the status of every horseman,"" or he said, ""Your companion wants to lower the status of every horseman and raise the status of every shepherd."" Upon this, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gathered his cloak and held it and said: ""Do I not see upon you the clothing of the foolish?"" Then he said: ""When the time of death of Allah's Prophet Nuh (peace be upon him) came, he said to his son: I am making a will to you. I command you with two things and forbid you from two things. I command you with «لا اله الا الله» , if the seven heavens and the seven earths were placed on one side of the scale and «لا اله الا الله» was placed on the other side, it would outweigh them. And if the seven heavens and the seven earths became a ring, «لا اله الا الله وسبحان الله وبحمده» would break it (in one narration: it would be its gem). This is the prayer of everything and by it everything is provided sustenance. And I forbid you from shirk and arrogance."" Upon this, I said or it was said: ""O Messenger of Allah! We have recognized shirk, but what is arrogance?"" Is arrogance that if one of us has a cloak, he wears it?"" He said: ""No."" It was asked: ""Is it that if one of us has very beautiful shoes and their laces are very beautiful?"" He said: ""No."" It was asked: ""Is it that one has a very good animal to ride upon?"" He said: ""No."" It was asked: ""That one has friends who sit with him respectfully?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is not it either."" It was asked: ""O Messenger of Allah! Then what is arrogance?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Rejecting the truth and looking down upon people."""
"427","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever considers himself great or walks with arrogance, he will meet Allah the Exalted in such a state that He will be angry with him."""
"428","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats with his servant, rides a donkey in the markets, and ties the legs of a goat to milk it, there is no arrogance in him."""
"429","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri and Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with them) that they narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Honor is Allah's lower garment and greatness is Allah's upper cloak. Whoever tries to take any of these two from Me, I will punish him."""
"430","It is narrated from Haithem bin Malik Tai that he said: I heard Nu'man bin Bashir saying on the pulpit: Indeed, Satan has traps and snares, and indeed, the traps and snares of Satan are to rebel (become arrogant) over the blessings of Allah, to boast over Allah's gifts, to show superiority over the servants of Allah, and to follow one's desires instead of Allah."
"431","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Paradise and Hell argued with each other,"" and Sufyan also said: ""Paradise and Hell quarreled. Hell said: 'The oppressors (and tyrants) will be gathered in me, and the arrogant will enter me.' And Paradise said: 'The weak will enter me, and the poor will enter me.' Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said to Paradise: 'You are My mercy; I will show mercy through you to whom I wish.' And He said to Hell: 'You are My punishment; I will punish through you whom I wish. And I will fill both of you.'"""
"432","It is narrated from Abu Salamah bin Abdur Rahman that he said: The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) were not people who would gather together, nor would they show themselves to be sick or weak (i.e., they did not pretend to be exhausted from worship). In their gatherings, they would recite poetry to each other and remember their days of ignorance. And when any one of them was called upon for something by the command of Allah, the pupils of his eyes would turn as if he were insane. (That is, they would become so anxious at Allah’s command that they would open their eyes wide and become fearful lest they fall short in acting upon it.)"
"433","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and he was handsome. He said: ""Love for being beautiful has been placed in my heart, and I have also been granted this (beauty) as you can see. I do not even like that anyone surpasses me in this (beauty), or he said, even by the strap of a shoe, or he said, by a red strap. Is this arrogance?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No, but arrogance is to reject the truth and to look down upon people."""
"434","Amr bin Shu’aib narrates from his father, and he from his grandfather, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “On the Day of Resurrection, the arrogant will be raised up like ants in the form of men. Humiliation will cover them from all sides. They will be driven to a prison in Hell called Boulas. The blazing fire will overpower them, and they will be given the pus of the wounds of the inhabitants of Hell to drink (i.e., lahuqachlu).”"
"435","It is narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: ""Go and take your recompense."""
"436","Narrated from Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: (Once) the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sent Lady Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). She sought permission (to enter) while he (peace and blessings be upon him) was with Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), wrapped in her sheet. He gave permission to Lady Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her), so she came in and said: ""Your wives have sent me; they are demanding justice from you regarding the daughter of Abu Quhafah."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O my daughter! Do you love whom I love?"" She said: ""Certainly."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Then love her (Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her)."" After that, she got up, went out, and informed the wives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). They said: ""You have not helped us at all. Go to him again."" She said: ""By Allah! I will never say anything to him about this again."" After that, they sent Lady Zainab (may Allah be pleased with her), the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). She sought permission from him, and he gave her permission as well. She also came and said the same thing to him, and along with that, she spoke harshly to me. So I began to look at (the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him) to see if he would permit me (to speak). I kept looking at him until I realized that if I responded, he would not mind. Then I also spoke about Zainab and prevailed over her, silencing her. At this, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) began to smile and then said: ""She is indeed the daughter of Abu Bakr."""
"437","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Ansar said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Divide these gardens between us and our brothers (the Muhajirun)."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No."" Upon this, the Ansar said: ""You take care of the expenses for us and we will make you partners in the fruit."" They said: (Very well) We have heard and we obey."
"438","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said during the year of famine, which was a year of severe drought, that Umar left no stone unturned in helping the villagers. He provided aid from camels, wheat, oil, and all kinds of produce. Until all the produce dried up due to the famine, at that time Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) began to supplicate: ""O Allah! Produce their sustenance on the tops of the mountains (i.e., snow and clouds)."" Allah accepted his and all the Muslims' supplication. When the rain fell, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Alhamdulillah! By Allah, if He had not removed this calamity, I would have seated the needy in every well-off Muslim household according to the number of family members, for the amount of food on which one person lives comfortably, two people can be saved from destruction."
"439","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Salamah bin Akwa’ (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “As for these sacrificial animals of yours, none of you should wake up on the third day while any of its meat remains with him.” When the next year came, they said: O Messenger of Allah! Should we do as we did last year? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Eat and store it, for last year the people were in hardship, so I wanted you to help them.”"
"440","It is narrated from Urwah who said: I was sitting with Sayyiduna Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him), something came to his mind so he was startled and said: Wisdom comes from experience. He said this three times."
"441","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I participated with my uncles in the Hilf al-Mutayyibeen (a pact of peace from the time of ignorance). I would not like to break this pact even in exchange for red camels."" (Mutayyibeen means those who applied perfume; Banu Hashim, Banu Zuhrah, and Banu Taym gathered in the house of Abdullah bin Jud'an, put perfume in a bowl, dipped their hands in it, and made this pact that they would help each other and ensure the rights of the poor and needy. They agreed that no one would be allowed to be oppressed or to oppress others there.)"
"442","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) established brotherhood between Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud and Sayyiduna Zubair (may Allah be pleased with them both)."
"443","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) established brotherhood between the Quraysh and the Ansar in my house, which is in Madinah."
"444","Amr bin Shu'aib narrates from his father, and he from his grandfather, that the Prophet (ﷺ) sat on the steps of the Ka'bah in the year of the conquest and praised Allah, then said: ""Whoever has a pact from the time of ignorance, Islam only strengthens it, and after the conquest of Makkah, there is no more migration."""
"445","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when we were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), rain fell upon us, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) removed his garment from his body until the rain fell upon him. We asked, ""Why did you do this?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied: ""Because it has just come from its Lord."""
"446","Humaid bin Malik bin Khuthaym narrates that I was sitting with Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) on his land in ‘Aqiq (at the end of the valley of ‘Aqiq is the gate of Madinah University), when some people from Madinah came to him riding on animals. Then they dismounted. Humaid narrates that Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Go to my mother and say to her, “Your son sends you salam and says, today please give us something to eat.” Upon this, his mother placed three loaves of barley bread and some olive oil and salt in a plate. I put it on my head and brought it to those people. When I placed the food before them, Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said “Allahu Akbar” and said: Praise be to Allah who has filled our stomachs with bread, while our food used to be nothing but the two black things, dates and water. The people did not eat anything from the food. When they left, he said: O my nephew, take good care of your goats, shake the dust off them, clean their pen, and pray in one corner of it. For these (goats) are among the animals of Paradise. By the One in whose hand is my soul, a time is near when a small flock of goats will be more beloved to its owner than Marwan’s palace (Marwan was a governor of Madinah)."
"447","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The center of disbelief is towards the east; pride and arrogance are found among the owners of horses and camels, and calmness (dignity) is found among the owners of goats."""
"448","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he said: I am amazed at dogs and goats. In one year, so many goats are slaughtered and so many are brought to Makkah for sacrifice (and goats are more numerous than dogs), even though a female dog gives birth to so many offspring. (It is Allah alone who has placed blessing in the goats.)"
"449","It is narrated from Abu Dhubyan that he said: Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said to me: O Abu Dhubyan! How much is your stipend? I said: Two and a half thousand. He said: O Abu Dhubyan! Engage in agriculture and animal breeding before the youths of Quraysh become your rulers; in their time, the stipend will not be considered wealth."
"450","‘Abdah bin Hazn says: The owners of camels and the owners of goats boasted to one another (the owners of camels said that they had superiority, and the owners of goats said that they had superiority). So the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “When Musa (Moses) was made a Prophet, he was a shepherd of goats; when Dawud (David) was made a Prophet, he too was a shepherd; and when I was made a Prophet, I used to graze the goats of my family in the Ajyad neighborhood.”"
"451","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: There are seven types of major sins, the first of which is: associating partners with Allah, killing a soul (unjustly), accusing chaste women of adultery, and adopting a Bedouin life after migration."
"452","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: ""Do not take up residence in the villages, for whoever resides in the villages is like one who lives in a graveyard."" Ahmad said: By «كفور» is meant: settlements (villages)."
"453","Shurayh narrates from his father that I asked Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) about going to the villages. I asked, ""Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ever go to the villages?"" She replied, ""Yes, he used to go to the villages towards those mounds."""
"454","It is narrated from Hasan al-Basri that when a man passed away, he left behind a son and a slave. He instructed his slave regarding his son (to take care of my son). The slave did not fall short in his care and upbringing until the boy reached maturity, and then he married him off. After that, the boy said to the slave: Prepare provisions for me so that I may set out to seek knowledge. The slave prepared the provisions, and the boy went to a scholar. He acquired knowledge from the scholar, and the scholar said: When you are about to leave, inform me so that I may teach you something. The boy said: Now the time for my departure has come, so please teach me. The scholar said: Fear Allah, be patient, and do not act hastily. Hasan (al-Basri) said: In these (three pieces of advice) is found all kinds of goodness. The boy returned, and it was unlikely that he would forget these words. There were only three, after all. When he came to his area, he dismounted from his ride. Then, when he entered his house, he saw a man sleeping a little distance from his wife, and his wife was also sleeping. He said: By Allah! I cannot think of waiting in the face of this scene. He returned to his mount. When he intended to take up his sword, he remembered: Fear Allah, be patient, and do not act hastily. Then he returned and stood over the sleeping man’s head, but thought, I cannot wait in this situation, so he returned to his mount. When he intended to pick up the sword, he remembered again, then returned and stood over his head. Then the man woke up. As soon as he saw him, he rushed to embrace him, kissed him, and asked about his well-being. He said: How was it after me? He replied: After you, it was very good, by Allah, very good, for that night I ran three times between the sword and your head, but the knowledge I had acquired stood in the way. (This man who was sleeping was his father’s freed slave, whom he did not recognize while he was sleeping, but when he woke up, he recognized him.)"
"455","It is narrated from Ashajj ‘Abdul Qais that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: “You have two qualities which Allah loves.” I asked: O Messenger of Allah! What are they? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Forbearance and modesty.” I asked: Are these qualities old or new in me? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “They are old.” I said: All praise is due to Allah, Who created me with two qualities which Allah loves."
"456","Sayyiduna Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that it was narrated to me by one who met the delegation of the tribe of Abdul Qais who came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Qatadah mentioned Abu Nadrah, who narrates from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), who said that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ashajj Abdul Qais: ""Indeed, there are two qualities in you which Allah loves: forbearance and patience."""
"457","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ashajj (i.e., Ashajj Abdul Qais): ""Indeed, there are two qualities in you which Allah loves: forbearance and deliberation in actions."""
"458","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that if one mountain were to wrong another mountain, the one committing the injustice would be shattered into pieces."
"459","Sayyiduna Fadala bin Ubaid (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""There are three types of people who will not be questioned: one is the person who separated himself from the congregation, disobeyed his leader, and died in a state of sin—do not ask about his condition (what will happen to him); the second is the slave or bondwoman who ran away from their master; the third is the woman whose husband is not at home, he provides for her worldly expenses, yet she goes out of the house adorned and mingles with men. There are three people who will not be questioned (i.e., they are outright criminals): the person who snatches Allah’s upper garment from Him—indeed, Allah’s upper garment is majesty, and His lower garment is honor; the second is the person who is doubtful and skeptical about Allah; and the third is the one who despairs of Allah’s mercy."""
"460","Bakar bin Abdul Aziz narrates from his father, and he from his grandfather (Abu Bakrah), and he from the Prophet (peace be upon him) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Of all the sins, the punishment for which Allah may defer until the Day of Resurrection, except for oppression, disobedience to parents, and severing ties of kinship. Such a person Allah gives swift punishment in this world before death."""
"461","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: One of you sees the speck in his brother’s eye, but forgets the large log (beam) or the trunk of a date-palm in his own eye. Abu Ubaid said: By «الجذل» is meant: a large and tall piece of wood."
"462","It is narrated from Muawiyah bin Qurrah that he said: I was with Ma’qil Muzani, and he removed something harmful from the road. I also saw something and hastened to remove it. Upon this, Ma’qil said: O my nephew! Why did you do that? I said: I saw you doing something, so I did it too. He said: O my nephew! You did well. I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say: “Whoever removes something harmful from the path of the Muslims, a good deed is written for him, and whoever has even one good deed accepted will enter Paradise.”"
"463","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Give gifts to one another, for this will create mutual love among you."""
"464","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say: ""O my sons! Exchange gifts with one another, for this increases love among you."""
"465","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man from Banu Fazarah gave a she-camel as a gift to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gave him something in return, but the man became displeased with it. Upon this, I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) saying from the pulpit: ""One of them gives me a gift, I give him in return according to what I have, then he becomes displeased with it. By Allah! After this, I will not accept a gift from any Arab except a Qurayshi, Ansari, Thaqafi, or Dosi."""
"466","It is narrated from Abu Mas’ud ‘Uqbah that he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Indeed, from what the people have received from the words of the previous Prophethood is this: If you feel no shame, then do whatever you wish.”"
"467","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Faith has over sixty or seventy branches, the most excellent of which is «لا اله الا الله» , and the lowest is removing something harmful from the road, and modesty is a branch of faith."""
"468","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was more modest than a veiled virgin girl. When he disliked something, we could recognize it from his face."
"469","Sayyiduna Uthman and Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with them) narrate that Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to enter. At that time, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was lying on Sayyidah Aisha’s (may Allah be pleased with her) bed, wrapped in her sheet. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) granted Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) permission while he was in that state. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) fulfilled his need and then left. After that, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) sought permission; the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) also granted him permission while he was in the same state. He fulfilled his need and then left. Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Then I sought permission from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), so he sat up properly and said to Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), “Gather your clothes.” She said: I fulfilled my need with you and then I left. Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: O Messenger of Allah! I noticed that you did not make the same arrangement for Abu Bakr and Umar as you did for Uthman. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: “Uthman is a very modest man. I feared that if I allowed him to enter in that state, he would not be able to express his need to me.”"
"470","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Modesty beautifies whatever it is in, and indecency makes whatever it is in defective."""
"471","Salim narrates from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by a man who was advising his brother about modesty (he was angry with him and scolding him), to the extent that he was saying: ""You are so modest that it is harming you."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Leave him, for indeed modesty is part of faith."""
"472","Narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her): She said, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was lying down in my house and he had uncovered his thigh or both his shins. At that moment, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) sought permission to enter. He allowed him to enter in that same state, and he came in and spoke. After that, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) sought permission. He also allowed him to enter in that same state, and he came in and spoke. After that, Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) sought permission. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sat up and adjusted his clothes. Muhammad (the narrator) said: I do not say that all three came on the same day. They entered and spoke, then when they left, Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I said, O Messenger of Allah! Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) came, you did not move or pay attention, then Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) came, you did not move or pay attention, but when Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) came, you sat up and adjusted your clothes? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Should I not show modesty to the one before whom even the angels are modest?”"
"473","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the noble son of the noble, son of the noble, son of the noble: Yusuf, son of Yaqub, son of Ishaq, son of Ibrahim (were such). (That Ibrahim) who was the close friend (Khalil) of the Most Merciful, Blessed and Exalted."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If I had remained in prison for as long as Yusuf did, and then the one who called (to release me) had come, I would have accepted his word and gone out. When the messenger came to him, he said: «ارجع إلى ربك فاسئله ما بال النسوة التى قطعن أيديهن» 'Return to your master and ask him what is the case of those women who cut their hands?' And may Allah have mercy on Lut, surely he sought refuge in a strong support. When he said to his people: «لو أن لي بكم قوة أو ءاوي إلى ركن شديد» 'Would that I had some power against you, or could take refuge in a strong support,' then after him, Allah did not send any prophet except that he (the prophet) had a large number of people (followers) with him."" Muhammad bin Umar, the narrator of this hadith, said: By ""tharwat"" is meant a large number and protectors."""
"474","It is narrated from Abdur Rahman bin Yazid that he said: Rabi’ used to come to Alqamah on Fridays. When I was not there, he would send a message to me. Once he came and I was not there, so Alqamah met me and said: Have you not seen what Rabi’ says? He says: Do you not see how much people supplicate and how little is accepted? This is because Allah does not accept any supplication except the pure ones. I said: Did Abdullah not say the same? He said: What did Abdullah say? He said that Abdullah narrated: Allah does not accept the supplication of a person who seeks fame, is a show-off, or supplicates jokingly. He only accepts the supplication that comes sincerely from the heart. The narrator said that Alqamah also mentioned this. He said: Yes."
"475","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When any one of you makes supplication, he should not say, '(O Allah) if You will, then grant it,' but he should supplicate with determination and increase his request, for nothing is too great for Allah to give."""
"476","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When any one of you supplicates, he should do so with full determination, and he should not say (and in one narration: When you supplicate to Allah, supplicate with full determination, and none of you should say): 'O Allah! If You wish, give me,' because there is no one who can compel Allah."""
"477","(Ikrimah) narrates from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), and he thinks that he himself heard from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that she saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raising both hands in supplication. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was saying «اللهم ! إنما أنا بشر فلا تعاقبني، أيما رجل من المؤمنين آذيته أو شتمته فلا تعاقبني فيه» ""O Allah! I am only a human being, do not punish me. If I have caused harm or spoken harshly to any of the Muslims, then do not punish me for that."""
"478","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that Sayyiduna Tufail bin Amr Dausi (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! The tribe of Daus has disobeyed and refused (to accept Islam). Pray against them."" Upon this, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) faced the Qiblah and raised his hands to pray. The people thought that he would pray against those people, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: «اللهم! اهدِ دوساً، وائت بهم» ""O Allah! Guide the tribe of Daus and bring them to me."""
"479","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that one year no rain fell (and there was a famine), so some Muslims stood before the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) on a Friday and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! The rain has been withheld, the land has become barren, and the livestock have perished."" Upon this, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) raised his hands; there was not a trace of cloud in the sky. He spread his hands even more until I saw the whiteness of his armpits. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed to Allah for rain. We had not even finished the Friday prayer when the young men from the nearest houses began to worry about returning to their homes. It rained continuously until the next Friday. When the next Friday came, someone said, ""O Messenger of Allah! The houses are collapsing and the caravans have stopped."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) smiled and said that the son of Adam becomes weary so quickly. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gestured with his hand: «اللهم ! حوالينا، ولا علينا"". فتكشطت عن المدينة» ""O Allah! Let the rain fall around us, not upon us."" So the clouds cleared away from Madinah."
"480","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, used to seek refuge and would say: «اللهم ! إني أعوذ بك من الكسل، وأعوذ بك من الجبن، وأعوذ بك من الهرم، وأعوذ بك من البخل» ""O Allah! I seek refuge in You from laziness, I seek refuge in You from cowardice, I seek refuge in You from extreme old age, and I seek refuge in You from miserliness."""
"481","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said: I am as My servant thinks of Me, and I am with him when he calls upon Me."""
"482","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he said: We used to count the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) reciting this supplication one hundred times in a single gathering: «رب اغفر لي وتب عليّ، إنك أنت التواب الرحيم» ""O Lord! Forgive me and accept my repentance. Indeed, You are the Acceptor of repentance, the Most Merciful."""
"483","It is narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) offered the Duha prayer, then said: «اللهم اغفر لي، وتب علي، إنك أنت التواب الرحيم» ""O Allah! Forgive me, accept my repentance, indeed You are the Acceptor of repentance and the Most Merciful."" He continued to say this supplication one hundred times."
"484","Sayyiduna Shaddad bin Aws (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The chief of supplications for seeking forgiveness is that a person says: «اللهم أنت ربي ، لا إله إلا أنت ، خلقتني وأنا عبدك ، وأنا على عهدك ووعدك ما استعطت ، أعوذ بك من شر ما صنعتُ ، أبوءُ لك بنعمتك ، وأبوء لك بذنبي فاغفر لي؛ فإنه لا يغفر الذنوب إلا أنت» Whoever recites this supplication with certainty during the day and dies before evening, he will be among the people of Paradise; and whoever recites it at night with certainty and dies before morning, he will be among the people of Paradise."
"485","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Burdah (may Allah be pleased with him): I heard a man from Juhainah, Agharr, narrate from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Repent to Allah, for I myself repent to Allah a hundred times every day."""
"486","It is narrated from Ka'b bin 'Ujrah that he said: There are some words whose reciter is never unsuccessful. They are: «سبحان الله» , «الحمدلله» , «لا اله الا الله » , «الله اكبر» one hundred times. This hadith has been narrated as marfu' by Ibn Abi Anisah and 'Amr bin Qais."
"487","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him): The supplication of a brother made for the sake of Allah is accepted."
"488","It is narrated from Safwan bin Abdullah bin Safwan. Darda bint Abu Darda was in his marriage. He narrates that (once) I reached them (Abu Darda) in Syria and saw that Umm Darda was at home and Abu Darda was not there. Umm Darda asked me: ""Do you intend to perform Hajj this year?"" I said: ""Yes."" She said: ""Pray for good for us, the Prophet (ﷺ) used to say: 'The supplication of a Muslim man for his Muslim brother in his absence is accepted. An angel is appointed over his head; when he prays for good for his brother, the angel says: Ameen, and may you have the same.'"" Safwan narrated that after this, I met Abu Darda in the market, and he narrated the same. He used to narrate this (hadith) from the Prophet (ﷺ)."
"489","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: A man said, ""O Allah! Forgive me and Muhammad only, and no one else."" Upon this, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""You have restricted your supplication to many people."""
"490","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that he used to make this supplication in his prayers: «اللهم توفيني مع الأبرار، ولا تخلفني فى الأشرار، وألحقني بالأخيار» O Allah! Grant me death among the righteous, do not leave me among the wicked, and join me with the good people."
"491","Shaqiq narrated: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) would often supplicate with these words: «ربنا أصلح بيننا، واهدنا سبل الإسلام، ونجنا من الظلمات إلى النور، واصرف عنا الفواحش ما ظهر منها وما بطن، وبارك لنا فى أسماعنا وأبصارنا وقلوبنا وأزواجنا وذرّياتنا، وتب علينا إنك أنت التواب الرحيم، واجعلنا شاكرين لنعمتك، مثنين بها، قائلين بها، وأتممها علينا» O our Lord! Reconcile between us, set us upon the ways of Islam, deliver us from darkness into light, remove from us indecencies—those which are apparent and those which are hidden, bless our hearing, our sight, our hearts, our wives, and our children. Accept our repentance, indeed You are the Acceptor of repentance, the Most Merciful. Make us grateful for Your blessings, praising them, speaking of them, and complete this blessing for us."
"492","Sayyiduna Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) prayed for his brother, he would say: «جعل الله عليه صلاة قوم أبرار، ليسوا بظلمة ولا فجار، يقومون الليل، ويصومون النهار الله» May the mercy of the righteous descend upon him, those who are neither oppressors nor sinners, who stand in prayer at night and fast during the day."
"493","Amr bin Harith says that my mother took me to the service of the Prophet (peace be upon him), so he (peace be upon him) passed his hand over my head and prayed for my sustenance."
"494","Abdullah Rumi narrates from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: It was said to him that your brothers have come from Basra; they used to live in a corner of Basra so that you may supplicate to Allah for them. He said: «اللهم اغفر لنا وارحمنا، وآتنا فى الدنيا حسنة، وفي الآخرة حسنة، وقنا عذاب النار"". فاستزادوه، فقال مثلها، فقال: ""إن أوتيتم هذا، فقد أوتيتم خير الدنيا والآخرة» O Allah! Forgive us, have mercy on us, grant us goodness in this world and the Hereafter, and save us from the punishment of Hell. When the people desired more supplication than this, he repeated the same and said: If you are granted this, you have attained goodness in this world and the Hereafter."
"495","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, took hold of a branch and shook it, but its leaves did not fall. Then he shook it again, but still its leaves did not fall. Then, when he shook it a third time, its leaves fell. He said: «سبحان الله ، الحمد لله ، لا اله الاالله» Sins are shaken off in this way, just as a tree sheds its leaves."
"496","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked: O Messenger of Allah! Which supplication is the best? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ask Allah for pardon and well-being in this world and the Hereafter. Then that man came the next day and submitted: O Messenger of Allah! Which supplication is the best? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ask Allah for pardon and well-being in this world and the Hereafter. When you are granted well-being in this world and the Hereafter, you have attained success."
"497","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: The most beloved words to Allah are: «سبحان الله لا شريك له ، له الملك وله الحمد ، وهو على كل شيء قدير . لا حول ولا قوة إلا بالله ، سبحان الله وبحمده» ."
"498","Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that (one time) the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came to me while I was praying. He had some need, but I was delayed, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Aisha! Make complete and comprehensive supplications."" When I finished my prayer, I asked: O Messenger of Allah! What is a complete and comprehensive supplication? He said: Say: «اللهم إني أسألك من الخير كله، عاجله وآجله، ما علمت منه وما لم أعلم. وأعوذ بك من الشر كله عاجله وآجله، ما علمت وما لم أعلم. وأسألك الجنة وما قرب إليها من قول أو عمل، وأعوذ بك من النار وما قرب إليها من قول أو عمل، وأسألك مما سألك به محمد صلى الله عليه وسلم، وأعوذ بك مما تعوذ منه محمد صلى الله عليه وسلم، وما قضيت لي من قضاء فاجعل عاقتبه رشداً » ""O Allah! I ask You for every good, immediate and delayed, that which I know and that which I do not know, and I seek refuge in You from every evil, of this world and the Hereafter, that which I know and that which I do not know. I ask You for Paradise and for every word and deed that brings me closer to it, and I seek refuge in You from the Fire and from every word and deed that brings me closer to it. I ask You for all that Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) asked You for, and I seek refuge in You from all that Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) sought refuge from. And whatever decision You make for me, make its outcome good for me."""
"499","Sayyiduna Anas and Sayyiduna Malik bin Aws bin Hadthan (may Allah be pleased with them) narrate that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went out to relieve himself. At that time, he did not find anyone to accompany him, so Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) followed behind him carrying clods or a water jug. He found the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in a field in the state of prostration, so he moved aside and sat behind him. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) raised his head, he said: ""Umar! You did well that when you found me in prostration, you sat at a distance. Jibreel came to me and said: Whoever sends blessings upon you once, Allah will send ten mercies upon him and raise him by ten degrees."""
